hi I'm Evan Carmichael welcome to  another edition of modeling the masters  I believe that the fastest and most  effective way to grow a business is to  model the strategies of people who have  already done that what you're trying to  do so today we're going to look at how a  Vietnam vet started two different  businesses and failed but was determined  to become a success and not have to work  for somebody else he would eventually go  on to become one of the most successful  business writers of all time this is the  story of Rich Dad Poor Dad creator  Robert Kiyosaki and the top three  lessons you can learn from his success  Robert Kiyosaki is an American investor  businessman self-help author  motivational speaker and financial  literacy expert best known for his Rich  Dad Poor Dad book series after serving  in the Marine Corps as a helicopter  gunship pilot during the Vietnam War  Kiyosaki returned home to work as a  salesman for Xerox not wanting to work  for someone else for the rest of his  life  Kiyosaki had dreams of starting his own  business after unsuccessful stints  selling velcro wallets and t-shirts for  heavy metal rock bands Kiyosaki began  promoting the personal growth seminars  of marshall thurber called money and  knew when Thurber decided to retire  Kiyosaki took over the business and  began traveling the world to educate  people about financial strategies to  reach more people he decided to write  his first book which he self-published  Rich Dad Poor Dad Robert Kiyosaki is  written over 15 books and is sold over  26 million copies three of his books  have been on the best sellers list of  the Wall Street Journal USA Today and  the New York Times simultaneously and  he's a sought-after speaker who  continues to educate people on how to  understand their money even though  Robert Kiyosaki failed with his first  two businesses he was determined to  become a successful entrepreneur and he  kept at it he tapped into his passion  for teaching people about money and went  on to become more the most successful  business writers of all time to help you  grow your business  here are three action items that you can  learn from Robert Kiyosaki  oxygen atom number one make your money  work hard one bit of advice you to serve  me well with my business is don't spend  money until you're making it anybody can  spend money if I gave you a million  dollars today for your business I'm sure  you can come up with a million different  ways to spend it but not everyone can  make money bootstrapping should be your  mantra find ways to get product or  service out without spending money get  even just a few orders and prove that  people will buy what you're selling then  spend money on expanding your marketing  your money will be well invested because  you know you have something that works  until you start making some sales hustle  and put your sweat in - drumming up some  business  Kiyosaki believes that people go to  school to learn how to work hard for  money while he tries to teach people how  to have money work hard for them he  believes that for many people success is  working hard to lend a secure job at a  big company or government who look after  you until you retire that model might  have worked in the industrial age but  now in the information age people have  to look out for their own financial  security because you can no longer rely  on your employer to take care of you one  of the best ways of doing this he  believes is to create your own business  and become your own boss  according to Kiyosaki the poor and  middle class work for money the rich  have money work for them the rich buy or  create assets that work for them so they  don't have to an asset puts money in  your pocket and a liability takes money  from your pocket the rich understand the  difference and buy assets not  liabilities actually not a number to  mind your own business as entrepreneurs  we have to wear many hats  you're everything from the CEO to the  janitor when you start a business if you  want to grow your business properly and  have confidence in your decision making  you need to understand your numbers yes  it may be boring and outside your core  competencies at the beginning but when  you can understand your balance sheet  income statement and the numbers that  run your business you'll be in a much  better position to drive the company  forward it could be one of the best  investments that you ever make into  yourself and your business if you want  to achieve financial freedom  Kiyosaki believes that there are three  key lessons that you need to master  learn how to make money learn how to  manage it and learn how to invest it  he encourages people to keep their day  jobs until they're earning enough money  on the side or from their own business  or from investments to be able to quit  Kiyosaki also believes that money is a  base subject and that it's never too  late to start learning according to  Kiyosaki many people confuse a  profession with their business to become  financially secure people need to mind  their own business  your business revolves around your asset  column as opposed to your income column  the rich focus on their asset columns  while the poor and middle-class focus on  their income columns action auto number  three work to learn not for money if you  have inserted your business yet a great  piece of advice is to get a job or you  can learn the skills that you need to  succeed as an entrepreneur want to set  up your own auto shop go work for a  small auto shop learn the ins and outs  of how the business runs ask the  business owner to get involved in other  projects in addition to what you're  hired to do work extra hours and on the  weekends to over-deliver  and really understand how the business  works you'll first figure out if that  industry is for you or not and you'll  also make many of your rookie mistakes  while still getting paid by somebody  else  Kiyosaki credits much of his success as  an entrepreneur to his military  education you learn how to lead men into  battle make important decisions quickly  and be tough he translated those skills  and hiring excellent workers and leading  them into business battles he also  credits working for Xerox are teaching  them how to sell and how to accept and  move forward from rejection  according to Kiyosaki many entrepreneurs  fail to grow because they lack  leadership skills and rather than look  in the mirror they find it easier to  blame others blame is short for be lame  and you can't be an effective leader if  you're lame work to learn don't work for  money look for jobs that can help you  develop the skills of managing cash flow  systems and people rather than just pay  you well  so remember make your money work hard  mind your own business and work to learn  not for money to finish up this video I  wanted to share one of my favorite true  stories about Robert Kiyosaki and some  of his best quotes there was once a  friend of Kiyosaki whose  sixteen-year-old son  desperately wanted a new car his friends  had all been given one by their parents  and now this son expected nothing less  but it was not going to be that easy for  the boy his father had played Kiyosaki  his cash flow board game and he wanted  to teach his son a lesson in financial  management the father gave his son  $3,000 but forbade him from using it to  buy a car just yet at the same time he  gave his son a subscription to The Wall  Street Journal the father told his son  that only once he had earned an  additional six thousand dollars from  investments who then used $3,000 to buy  a car  the rest of the money would of course go  to into his college fund my friend said  it was the best three thousand dollars  he ever spent says Kiyosaki not only had  a son gained a new respect for the power  of money he also learned to spend money  wisely instead of letting money burn  holes in his pockets  you  you  you  thank you for joining me for another  dish of modeling masters if you liked  the video and you want to see more  please give it a thumbs up below  I'd also love to hear oh you have to  think if you want to leave a comment  under the video and stay tuned for next  episode  you  you
 

